{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788374630921,"sessionID":"ses_f9c90f27fffeQr9sSyaGoxWpAt","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-adf813a32a3a4236","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git -C ~/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-159 show --stat 45c76be"},"output":"commit 45c76bedb230aa116e19dbd1e30e47aee4ca4d94\nAuthor: Daniel Kantor <git@daniel-kantor.com>\nDate:   Tue Sep 1 23:26:58 2026 +0200\n\n    Retire input/inputs/lines for one stdin source with parse as a library call\n    \n    The stdin-syntax-design ruling (gh:159, tentative): three keywords become a\n    single raw Stream<Str> source named `stdin`, and reading a value is an\n    ordinary `parse(.)` call over it. The parser, checker, TIR, and every backend\n    now carry `stdin` and the `parse` builtin instead of the three source forms;\n    the host connects live stdin only when the program reads the source.\n    \n    Source migration only; the corpus and test files still spell the old keywords\n    and land in a follow-up.\n    \n    Human-authored: the single-source shape and parse-as-library-call semantics\n    Derived: per-backend parse emission from each target's native JSON handling\n    Agent-invented: the parse_read checked-form wiring in the checker\n    \n    Written by DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: DeepSeek V4 Flash via opencode <git@daniel-kantor.com>\n\n build.rs               |   5 +-\n runtime/toylang.c      | 149 +++--------------------\n src/ast.rs             |  21 +---\n src/check/linearity.rs |  10 +-\n src/check/mod.rs       | 254 +++++++++++----------------------------\n src/emit_go.rs         | 127 ++++++++++----------\n src/emit_jq.rs         |  32 ++---\n src/emit_js.rs         |  43 ++-----\n src/emit_llvm.rs       | 114 ++++--------------\n src/emit_lua.rs        | 137 ++++++++++++++++------\n src/emit_py.rs         |  40 ++-----\n src/emit_rs.rs         | 120 ++++++-------------\n src/emit_toylang.rs    |   4 +-\n s